# C# conventions (summary of docs/09-coding-standards.md)

- File-scoped namespaces matching folders (`ProdTrack.Application.WorkOrders.Release`); one public type per file.
- Nullable enabled; no `!` suppression without a comment explaining why.
- `sealed` by default; `record` for DTOs/commands/value objects; primary constructors for DI in services/handlers.
- Async all the way with `CancellationToken ct` as last parameter; no `.Result`, `.Wait()`, `async void`.
- Inject `TimeProvider`; never `DateTime.Now/UtcNow`. Timestamps are `DateTimeOffset` UTC named `...AtUtc`.
- Structured logging templates (`"Operation {OperationId} started"`), never string interpolation in log calls; never log secrets or tokens.
- Guard clauses with `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull` etc. Exhaustive `switch` expressions over enums with `UnreachableException` default.
- Expose `IReadOnlyList<T>`/`IReadOnlyCollection<T>` from entities; keep setters private.
- Handlers return `Result`/`Result<T>` with typed errors (`WorkOrderErrors.ArtworkNotApproved`, code `WorkOrder.ArtworkNotApproved`). Throw only for truly exceptional situations.
- EF Core: `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` per entity; `AsNoTracking()` + projections for queries; no lazy loading; no concatenated SQL.
- Endpoints: `MapGroup("/api/v1/...")`, `TypedResults`, `.RequireAuthorization(Policies.X)`, `.WithName()/.WithSummary()`, declare `Produces`/`ProducesProblem`.
- Mapping: Mapperly or explicit mapping methods; no AutoMapper.
- Packages only via `Directory.Packages.props`; avoid commercially licensed packages (FluentAssertions v8+, MediatR v13+, AutoMapper).
- `TODO` comments must include a story key: `// TODO PT-061: ...`.
